# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. Never commit `.env`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# PostgreSQL connection string used by Prisma (schema: prisma/schema.prisma).
# PostgreSQL >= 15 is required.
# For pooled providers (Supabase/Neon) use the pooler host and keep
# `sslmode=require` so migrations and the app can connect.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database?sslmode=require"

# Public base URL of the running app. Used by the better-auth browser client
# (lib/auth/auth-client.ts). Falls back to http://localhost:3000 in development.
# Must include the scheme (https://...). A bare domain without a scheme throws
# ERR_INVALID_URL inside better-auth during the production build.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Secret used by better-auth to sign sessions/cookies.
# Generate one with: npx @better-auth/cli secret
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# Server-side base URL better-auth uses for callbacks/redirects.
# Must include the scheme (https://...). A bare domain without a scheme throws
# ERR_INVALID_URL during the production build.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SMS provider seam — lib/auth/sms.ts (sms.ir Verify integration)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTP codes are delivered through sms.ir's Verify API (lib/auth/sms.ts).
# While SMSIR_API_KEY stays unset the development mock ([DEV OTP] ...) is used,
# and production refuses to run without a real key.
#
# To go live with sms.ir:
#   1. Create a Sandbox API key via sms.ir panel:
#      برنامه‌نویسان → لیست کلیدهای API → ایجاد کلید جدید (type: Sandbox)
#      → copy it into SMSIR_API_KEY below (and locally in .env).
#   2. The Sandbox only supports the fixed Verify template "123456" whose text
#      is "کد تایید شما: #CODE#". This is SMSIR_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_ID's default.
#      Before going to production you MUST:
#        a. Create a real production API key (type: Production) and set it as
#           SMSIR_API_KEY.
#        b. Create a real production Verify template in the sms.ir panel and
#           set its ID as SMSIR_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_ID (replace the "123456" default).
#   3. Never commit real values of these variables — keep them out of version
#      control and set them in Vercel / your hosting environment.
SMSIR_API_KEY=""
SMSIR_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_ID="123456"